# Pinned opencode release checksums, one line per version and platform.
# Archive SHA-256 values come from the anomalyco/homebrew-tap formula `opencode-v2.rb`.
# Binary SHA-256 is the `opencode` file inside the archive (also used to verify a local fallback copy). Both are
# required: Scripts/make-app.sh bundles only an opencode whose SHA-256 equals the binary column (D2).
# Source: `homebrew` when the archive digest matched the tap's formula for that version, `first-seen` when only the
# observed digest is recorded (no published one); a human confirms a first-seen line before the pin moves to it.
# Lines are written by Scripts/opencode-upgrade.sh (docs/features/opencode-upgrades.md).
#
# version  platform              archive-sha256                                                    binary-sha256                                                     source
